From c454c55a687d0453085addcc0b96d07137d82668 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: reaper <theunbounddeveloper@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 1 Aug 2026 09:47:47 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] reaper v2.0.1: gate benign blog_get_dstentry_by_id KERN_DEBUG
 syslog flood

The Broadcom flow accelerator logs two KERN_DEBUG lines in
blog_get_dstentry_by_id() when a live flow references a dst-entry id whose
128-slot table entry has been recycled ("match fails entry.dstid[id+128]", and
the zero user_count variant). Both are self-correcting: the function returns
NULL and the caller (bcm_tcp_accel) simply re-learns the flow on the slow path.
On every accelerator rebuild (restart_qos / restart_firewall / wireless Apply)
active flows briefly hold stale ids, so these fire in bursts and flood syslog.

This build ships BusyBox klogd/syslogd (RTCONFIG_RSYSLOGD unset), which forwards
the whole kernel ring buffer to the log with no severity or content filter --
so console_loglevel and any userspace rule cannot drop just these lines, and a
developer running at debug level gets the flood mixed into everything else.

Gate both prints behind REAPER_BLOG_DSTENTRY_ID_DEBUG (default 0) so they are
dead-code-eliminated in normal builds (a hair cheaper than the rate-limited
print) while every other kernel/userspace debug message is untouched. Flip to 1
to restore them when specifically debugging dst-entry recycling. Stock Broadcom
behavior is otherwise unchanged (still returns NULL on the miss).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../kernel/bcmkernel/net/core/blog_dst.c             | 12 ++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/kernel/bcmkernel/net/core/blog_dst.c b/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/kernel/bcmkernel/net/core/blog_dst.c
index fb9753d25d..47d98fa22d 100644
--- a/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/kernel/bcmkernel/net/core/blog_dst.c
+++ b/release/src-rt-5.04behnd.4916/kernel/bcmkernel/net/core/blog_dst.c
@@ -1,5 +1,13 @@
 #include <net/dst.h>
 
+/* Reaper: the two lookup-miss diagnostics in blog_get_dstentry_by_id() below are
+ * self-correcting (the caller re-learns the flow on the slow path) and flood syslog
+ * on every accelerator rebuild (restart_qos/firewall/wireless). This build ships
+ * BusyBox klogd, which forwards the whole kernel ring buffer with no severity/content
+ * filter, so they cannot be dropped in userspace. Gate them here; set to 1 to restore
+ * the prints when debugging dst-entry recycling. */
+#define REAPER_BLOG_DSTENTRY_ID_DEBUG 0
+
 /*------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  *BLOG dst id map table and its related functions, adopted from bcmnetdev
  *-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------*/
@@ -254,11 +262,11 @@ struct dst_entry *blog_get_dstentry_by_id(uint16_t dstid)
             atomic_dec(&pentry->user_count);
             return dst;
         }
-        else
+        else if (REAPER_BLOG_DSTENTRY_ID_DEBUG)
             printk_ratelimited(KERN_DEBUG "%s:Trying to get dstentry pointer for idx[%d] dstid[%d] but zero user_count\n",
                     __FUNCTION__, idx, dstid);
     }
-    else
+    else if (REAPER_BLOG_DSTENTRY_ID_DEBUG)
     {
         printk_ratelimited(KERN_DEBUG "%s:dstid[%d] match fails entry.dstid[%d]\n",__FUNCTION__,
                 dstid, pentry->dstid.dstid);
-- 
